<P><FONT SIZE=2><B>Federal Income Tax Aspects  </B></FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The general partner expects that the Fund will be treated as a partnership and not as an association taxable as a corporation for federal income tax purposes, so
long as the Fund satisfies an annual gross income test, which the general partner anticipates that the Fund will satisfy. Accordingly, whether or not the Fund makes any distributions to you, you will
be required to report your share of income, gain, loss and deduction of the Fund and will be individually liable for federal and state income tax on that share. The gain or loss on the Fund's
investment in commodity interest contracts, depending on the contracts traded, will constitute a mixture of ordinary income or loss and capital gain or loss. Trading losses of the Fund, which will
generally constitute capital losses, may only be used to offset a limited amount of the ordinary income allocated to you, and the deductibility of Fund expenses may be subject to specified
limitations. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2><B>Reports to Limited Partners  </B></FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;You will receive monthly statements setting forth the value of your units and other information relating to the Fund's performance. Within 90&nbsp;days of the
end of each calendar year, you also will receive a certified annual report of the Fund together with the information necessary for you to prepare your annual income tax return. This certified annual
report will contain financial statements that have been audited by the Fund's independent accountants. </FONT></P>

