<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;May
performance was slightly negative for the Fund. The month started with good prospects for trendfollowers, but by month end those prospects had faded. Losses were generated in gold,
Euroswiss, Japanese yen and sugar as all of these sectors were marked by high volatility throughout May. Profits in natural gas and the Mexican peso somewhat softened these losses. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;June
was another month with negative performance for the Fund as tradable trends failed to materialize. Volatile, directionless price action in the Euroswiss, Euro and Australian
interest rate markets accounted for the bulk of the losses in June. While these losses were lessened by profits in lean hogs and soybeans, the second quarter closed with seemingly disjointed markets
