<BR></FONT><FONT SIZE=2><B>THE CLEARING BROKERS    <BR>  </B></FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Refco,&nbsp;Inc. serves as the Fund's clearing broker. It is expected that UBS PaineWebber will serve as an additional clearing broker upon commencement of this
offering. The following descriptions provide for each clearing broker background information and information regarding material legal proceedings involving the clearing broker. You should note that
the descriptions below were prepared by the clearing brokers. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For
ease of administration, the trading advisors may direct all or a portion of their trades on behalf of the Fund to executing brokers or floor brokers for execution with instructions
to give-up the executed trade to the clearing broker for clearing and settlement. The cost of any give-up fees to brokers will be included in the Fund's brokerage charge. The Fund's
over-the-counter options, forward, swap and spot contracts generally will be transacted through the clearing brokers or their affiliates. The trading advisors also from time to
time may select other dealers through which such contracts will be traded, but only with the prior written consent of the general partner. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2><B>Refco  </B></FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2><B><I>General  </I></B></FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Refco,&nbsp;Inc. has served as the Fund's clearing broker since the Fund began trading in January&nbsp;1989. The address of Refco's principal office is 550
West Jackson Boulevard, Suite 1300, Chicago, Illinois 60661 and its telephone number is (312)&nbsp;788-2000. Refco is registered under the Commodity Exchange Act as a futures commission
merchant and is a member of the NFA. It also is a member of certain principal U.S. futures exchanges. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Refco
provides commodity interest brokerage and clearing services to the Fund. It is not a sponsor, general partner or selling agent for the Fund, and the only relationship that it has
with the Fund is that of broker for executing and clearing the Fund's commodity interest transactions. Refco does not have
or accept any discretionary authority with respect to transactions or investments in the Fund's trading account. Refco may use the services of other clearing brokers and brokers who are members of
exchanges of which Refco is not a member. Refco maintains the trading account of the Fund on its books and records as a separate account. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2><A
NAME="dw2420_conflicts_of_interest"> </A>
<A NAME="toc_dw2420_2"> </A>
<BR></FONT><FONT SIZE=2><B><I>Conflicts of Interest    <BR>  </I></B></FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Refco is presently acting as clearing broker for other commodity pools, providing services similar to those provided the Fund, and expects to continue to serve in
this capacity for commodity pools in the future. Refco also serves a number of other non-commodity pool customers. Its responsibilities to the Fund and the responsibilities that it has or
may undertake in the future may cause a conflict of interest. These conflicts may result in competition among commodity pools and other customers for services provided to them by the clearing broker.
In addition, Refco may in the future charge other customers, including public and private commodity pools, a lower brokerage rate than is being charged to the Fund. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;An
affiliate of Refco, Refco Securities LLC, has in the past, and may in the future, serve as a selling agent for the Fund. Because Refco's compensation as clearing broker is based, at
least in part, on the net asset value of the Fund, Refco Securities LLC, may have a conflict of interest between acting in the best interest of its clients when advising them to purchase or redeem
units and assuring continued compensation to Refco. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Refco
and its principals, employees and agents may trade commodity interest contracts for their own accounts. These trades may be different from, opposite to or entered ahead of trades
entered into by the Fund, and these persons may even be the other party to a trade entered into by the Fund. The records of any of these trades will not be available to limited partners. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2><B><I>Legal Proceedings  </I></B></FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Except as follows, Refco has advised the general partner that, as of the date of this prospectus, during the preceding five years neither Refco nor any of its
principals have been the subject of any material administrative, civil or criminal action, whether pending, on appeal, or concluded. </FONT></P>

