<P><FONT SIZE=2><B><I>Brokerage Charge  </I></B></FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Fund will pay the general partner a monthly charge of 0.675%, or 8.1% annually, of the Fund's net asset value. The general partner pays from the brokerage
charge all clearing, execution and give-up, floor brokerage, exchange and NFA fees, any other transaction costs, selling agent compensation and consulting fees to the trading advisors. The
payments to the clearing brokers will be based upon a specified amount per round-turn for each commodity interest transaction executed on behalf of the Fund. The amounts paid to selling
agents, trading advisors or others may be based upon a specified percentage of the Fund's net asset value or round-turn transactions. A round-turn is both the purchase, or
sale, of a commodity interest contract and the subsequent offsetting sale, or purchase, of the contract. The balance of the brokerage charge not paid out to other parties shall be retained by the
general partner as payment for its services to the Fund. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The
Fund pays the general partner the brokerage charge, which is based on a fixed percentage of net assets, regardless of whether actual transaction costs were less than or exceeded this
fixed percentage. Assuming the Fund's brokerage costs were expressed on a per-transaction basis, it is estimated that the Fund's 8.1% annual brokerage charge would equate to
round-turn commissions of $48.00 during 2004, based on the Fund's current selection of trading advisors. The round-turn equivalent of the Fund's brokerage charge will vary with
the frequency with which the trading advisors place orders for the Fund's account managed by each of them. </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The
Fund is required by certain state securities administrators to disclose that the brokerage charge payable by the Fund, as defined by the Guidelines for the Registration of Commodity
Pool Programs developed by the North American Securities Administrators Association,&nbsp;Inc., or NASAA Guidelines, will not be greater than (1)&nbsp;80% of the published retail commission rate
plus pit brokerage fees, or (2)&nbsp;14% annually of the Fund's average net assets, including pit brokerage fees. The general partner intends to operate the Fund so as to comply with these
limitations. No material change in the amount of the brokerage charge will made unless notice </FONT></P>

